-**Hacking SES-imagotag VUSION 2.6 BWR GL440 (EDG2-0260-A) e-ink tag**
 - MCU = TI CC2510 (8051 + 2.4GHz GFSK, 32KB flash). Display = Pervasive Displays EL026TR3 (296x152 BWR, IL0373).
-- Route 1 (recommended): flash custom firmware `prime-axiom/gl440-client-firmware` + `gl440-ap-firmware` AP. Flash via ESP32 + `atc1441/ESP_CC_Flasher` (Wi-Fi AP CC_Flasher/12345678, UI at cc.local). Debug pads DD/DC/RST/GND/VCC → GPIO23/19/33. 3.3V only. Back up .hex before erase (CRP blocks read, chip erase bypasses but destroys firmware).
+- Route 1 (recommended): flash custom firmware prime-axiom/gl440-client-firmware + gl440-ap-firmware AP. Flash via ESP32 + atc1441/ESP_CC_Flasher (Wi-Fi AP CC_Flasher/12345678, UI at cc.local). Debug pads DD/DC/RST/GND/VCC → GPIO23/19/33. 3.3V only. Back up .hex before erase (CRP blocks read, chip erase bypasses but destroys firmware).
 - Route 2: bypass CC2510, drive panel directly via SPI from ESP32/RP2040. GL440 has test pads for 6 display pins on back. Walkthrough: blog.jirkabalhar.cz/2023/12/hacking-sesimagotag-e-ink-price-tag/
 - Route 3: voltage glitch CC2510 CRP bypass: zeus.ugent.be/blog/22-23/reverse_engineering_epaper
 - Note: VUSION 2.6 has other variants (e.g. UU340 = AX8052 868MHz), GL440 is the CC2510 one.
 
